      "text": "[3:55PM] #OkotaIsolo #TrafficUpdate \n\nCele to Pako Stretch: Traffic is moving smoothly in both directions.\n\nCele Link Bridge to Ijesha: Both inbound and outbound routes are clear and free-flowing.\n\nNwachukwu Drive (inner section) to Cele: No delays in either direction; traffic is steady.\n\nAgo Palace Road to Apple Junction: Traffic is light and movement is encouraging in both directions.\n\nIbeh Road Apata to Transformer Junction, Ilasa Underbridge (Service Lane): Free-flowing traffic both inbound and outbound.\n\nInner Ire-Akari Road to Osolo Road: Movement remains smooth in both directions.\n\nOke Afa to Pako, Kogberegbe, Ile Ibadan, Ishaga College, Omonide, Aye, Limca Junction: Inbound traffic towards Lasutech Roundabout and onward to Daleko Bridge is experiencing slow movement due to market-related congestion at Daleko.\n\nFive Star, Iyana Isolo, and Iyana Itire: Inbound traffic to Ijesha Express—both on the main carriageways and service lanes—is currently moving well with no reported delays.\n\nOur men are present at key locations ensuring ease of traffic movement. \n\n#FollowLASTMA",
